Changes to Zwall....
--------------------

Version 1.0
-----------
First release - February 1995

Version 1.1
-----------
Fixed in the (T) and (B) keys for top and bottom entry in the wall.

Fixed up a slight bug where the changed colours weren't being saved in
the users prefs file unless they edited their signature as well.

Optimised some of the routines to functions to save duplication, and also
shortened some stupid extranous loops etc which weren't nescessary with a
little thought :)

Implemented the Return Skip option for the config file and in the 
program. Optional now to allow return to exit the Wall or not.

Changed the default Ansi a bit to show new options. Fixed up the option 
to use your own Ansi for Zwall main screen if you so wish. Be careful not
to change too much as the ansi positions on a lot of the data are hard
coded into the program.. You may wanna do a nicer logo for Zwall or 
whatever, as mine is pretty crap :-)

Nasty bits of opening and closing files were sometimes using Call and
some of them were not.. Bit dicey that although it didn't cause problems
utill now here :-) Fixed!

Top Poster file is now parsed and updated accordingly when someone sprays
a message on the wall. User is informed if they become the top poster
after they spray some text.

When a message is deleted the program now scans the writer of the message
data file, and takes one of their total postings off. It then also scans
the top poster file and if they are the current top poster, then it will
remove one number from that as well. I think that makes it work totally
accuratly anyway. If someone comes on and writes a message who now has a
higher number of posts than the top poster, it will give them the title
anyway.. If they don't spray a message though then it won't do it.. Maybe
I should make a check on this as soon as they enter the wall :-)

Version 1.2
-----------
Fixed a bug in the delete message routine which would exit the
script when changing the user who's message got deleted number
of postings.

Version 1.3
-----------
Fixed up some logfile problems if it didn't exist to start with. It would
not log anything at all. Bad programing on my part. It now creates a new
logfile if one isn't present so periodic deleting is not a problem.

Done a few changes on starting the wall so there's a slight
speed increase.

Fixed a minor bug in the top poster routine. It would update by 2 if there
was a message deleted which the top poster had written, and they posted another
one. You would not believe how hard it was to track this bloody thing down.

No longer displays the intro message about prefs found or not found. As it's all
automatic the user doesn't need to know about it and think something is wrong.

Zwall will inform when a deleted message is removed and can't find the prefs file
of the original poster. It won't stop running if this happens and it isn't 
serious. It just means it can't adjust their number of total postings on the
wall in their userdata. It's not likely to happen unless you've deleted user
prefs files manually.

The Zwall Purge function has now been fixed so that all user prefs files will
be updated after the wall has been reset to change their number of posts to 0
again. At last :-) Also it will give a graphic display so you know something
is going on. Always a good idea.

Changed the delete message routine to add in a display routine so you know that
something is happening when it goes through the hefty shuffle routine needed to
remove a message.

Fixed some nasty dupe variable names which could have affected logfile entries.
Also took out the dodgy variable names while I was at it :)

Reworked the display code so that wrong keypresses did not redisplay the Wall
text.. Looked messy and slow before. Now it's fine.

Incorporated the Banned users config - See example config with archive. All
you need to do is add someones name to this text config and they won't be
able to use the Zwall anymore on logon. Works perfectly. Will log a message in
the Logfile if it can't find a Zwall.ban file but ignores the checking.

Fixed a small bug where Cosysop access was hard coded for 99 instead of taken
from the config file when displaying users real name. The kind of bug that would
not normally show up unless it was on another BBS :-)

You can now quit entering text on any line by pressing return on an unedited
line, or typing q and then return.

